  "question": {
    "text": "Consider a square matrix <math><mi>A</mi></math> of order <math><mn>2</mn></math> which has its elements as <math><mn>0,1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2,4</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If the absolute value of <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is least then, the absolute value of <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
